# Build context for backend/Dockerfile, which is built from the repo root.
#
# An allow-list: only what the image copies is sent to the builder. Everything
# else -- .env and its keys, data/ (~750MB of release tarballs), node_modules,
# .git -- never leaves the machine.
*
!backend
!configs
!experiments

**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.cache
backend/tests
